<!-- Material Symbols "outbox" (filled). The Outbox row above the accounts (docs/sending.md).
     Vendored from google/material-design-icons; the Compose `Icon` supplies the real
     colour, so the fillColor here is only a placeholder.

     Its own glyph rather than "send": that one is already the Sent folder's, and an Outbox
     drawn as Sent is the one confusion this row exists to prevent.

     The group translate is the source's own coordinate system rather than a hand-transformed
     path. Material Symbols draws in a `0 -960 960 960` viewBox, so every absolute y is
     negative; shifting the whole group down by 960 is exactly that viewBox, and it leaves the
     path data as upstream published it, where a retyped one is a glyph nobody would notice was
     subtly wrong. -->
